explanation:
The body is `(if 0 < x 0 then 1 else 2 : ℝ) • 1`, with `1` the identity matrix in `Matrix (Fin (n+1)) (Fin (n+1)) ℝ`. This is exactly κ(x)·I, with κ = 1 on the open half-space {x₀ > 0} and κ = 2 on its complement, including the hyperplane itself, as the docstring says.

Writing the dimension as n+1 is needed so that the coordinate x₀ exists. It does not make the definition too narrow, because this is a single explicit example used to illustrate De Giorgi's theorem with discontinuous coefficients. Mathlib has no matching declaration.

The file's lemmas confirm the intended properties:
- the field is uniformly elliptic with constants 1 and 2;
- it is measurable;
- it is discontinuous at every point of {x₀ = 0}.
